  "__readme": "Parity fixtures for TurnOutcomeRecord (shared/turn-outcome.ts) across repos. Kept in lockstep with mcpjam-backend (tests/convex/fixtures/turn-outcome-parity-fixtures.json) and pinned in convex/lib/mirrors.json. The backend cannot import this repo's Zod (Convex bundling isolation), so this JSON is the common ground truth: turnOutcomeRecordZ must parse every 'accept' row and refuse every 'reject' row, and the backend's parseTurnOutcomeRecord() must reach the SAME verdict on each. A producer emitting a record the backend refuses would be silently stripped at ingest and the turn would read as 'unrecorded' — which is why the backend deploys first. The 'reject' rows are the contract's invariants, one per row: a timed_out with no clock is the bare 'aborted' this contract replaces; a completed carrying a termination claims both that it finished and that something ended it.",
